\description{
Builds every registered deliverable in one call from a prepared
\code{ctdna_prep} object. Each step is opt-in via the modalities
present on the prep: steps whose required frame is missing are
skipped with a clear reason; steps that error are captured (never
halt the pipeline) with the full error message for later review.
}
\details{
\strong{The registry.} A single internal step registry maps every
short name (\code{"baseline"}, \code{"reduction"},
\code{"longitudinal"}, \code{"oncoprint"}, ...) to (a) the plot
function it calls, (b) the prep slot(s) it needs, and (c) the
default arguments it uses. \code{\link{ctdna_pipeline_steps}}
returns this as a data frame so callers can see the current
catalog without running anything. \code{which =} takes any subset
of those keys.

\strong{No silent failures.} Every step either lands in
\code{$plots$<key>} (success) or in one of two named slots:
\code{$failures$<key>} if the plot function errored (value = the
exact error message), or \code{$skipped$<key>} if a required prep
slot was missing (value = a string naming the missing slot).

\strong{Per-plot overrides.} Every plot's registry defaults can be
overridden with \code{overrides = list(<key> = list(...))}. For
example \code{overrides = list(baseline = list(method = "maxvaf"))}
passes \code{method = "maxvaf"} into \code{ctdna_plot_baseline()}
while leaving every other step at its default.
}
\examples{
sim  <- ctdna_make_mock_study(n_patients = 20, seed = 1)
prep <- ctdna_prepare(
  infinity_report = sim$infinity_report,
  adam            = list(adsl = sim$clinical),
  verbose         = FALSE)
prep <- ctdna_sample_qc(prep, verbose = FALSE)

# Run every step whose modalities are present in this minimal prep.
out <- ctdna_pipeline(prep, verbose = FALSE)
print(names(out$plots))    # every successful step
print(out$skipped)         # which steps were skipped (and why)
print(out$timing)          # seconds per step

# Run only a subset, with per-step overrides:
out_sub <- ctdna_pipeline(prep,
  which     = c("baseline", "reduction"),
  overrides = list(baseline  = list(method = "maxvaf"),
                   reduction = list(metric = "tf")),
  verbose   = FALSE)
print(names(out_sub$plots))

# Dry-run: see what would run without building anything.
dry <- ctdna_pipeline(prep, dry_run = TRUE, verbose = FALSE)
print(dry)
}
